WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.884 --> 00:00:18.145
the princess cried to the children.

2
00:00:18.165 --> 00:00:20.506
"I have been gone too long!

3
00:00:21.507 --> 00:00:23.548
By now the servants will be looking for me!"

4
00:00:25.469 --> 00:00:30.272
When they reached a courtyard, several servants rushed toward the princess.

5
00:00:31.888 --> 00:00:33.589
"Where have you been, Your Highness?"

6
00:00:34.089 --> 00:00:35.150
cried one woman.

7
00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.271
"Your Highness!"

8
00:00:37.772 --> 00:00:39.252
Another servant gasped.

9
00:00:40.253 --> 00:00:41.754
"Who are these strangers?

10
00:00:42.674 --> 00:00:43.835
Did they kidnap you?"

11
00:00:43.855 --> 00:00:47.077
"No, they did not kidnap me!"

12
00:00:47.577 --> 00:00:48.858
the princess replied.

13
00:00:48.878 --> 00:00:52.160
"They helped me," she added.

14
00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:55.142
"And now they are my honored guests."

15
00:00:56.282 --> 00:00:59.084
The servants did not look happy to hear this.

16
00:01:00.304 --> 00:01:03.386
But they bowed quietly and then stepped aside.

17
00:01:04.827 --> 00:01:08.449
The children followed the princess into a small building.

18
00:01:09.509 --> 00:01:12.871
She invited them to sit around a low table.

19
00:01:13.952 --> 00:01:17.114
Then she left for a moment to change her clothing.

20
00:01:18.814 --> 00:01:22.296
Mandy noticed a sheet of paper with unusual writing.

21
00:01:22.316 --> 00:01:25.678
"Are these Chinese characters?"

22
00:01:26.239 --> 00:01:28.360
she asked when the princess returned.

23
00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:31.570
"No," said the princess.

24
00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:35.994
"That is Hangeul, the alphabet that my father invented."

25
00:01:36.014 --> 00:01:39.978
"Your father invented an alphabet?"

26
00:01:40.478 --> 00:01:41.219
said Mandy.

27
00:01:41.239 --> 00:01:44.221
"Yes," said the princess.

28
00:01:44.241 --> 00:01:47.725
"Our people have always spoken in Korean.

29
00:01:48.826 --> 00:01:51.728
But they used Chinese characters to read and write.

30
00:01:52.909 --> 00:01:55.732
Chinese characters were very difficult to learn.

31
00:01:56.836 --> 00:01:59.678
And only nobles could go to school to learn them."

32
00:01:59.698 --> 00:02:02.220
"That's not fair!"

33
00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:03.521
Mandy said.

34
00:02:03.541 --> 00:02:06.803
"I agree," said the princess.

35
00:02:06.823 --> 00:02:10.125
"My father didn't think it was fair either.

36
00:02:11.106 --> 00:02:14.988
That is why he worked with scholars to invent a simple alphabet.

37
00:02:16.389 --> 00:02:18.371
Hangeul is very easy to learn.

38
00:02:19.411 --> 00:02:22.073
And now the Korean people have their own alphabet."

39
00:02:22.093 --> 00:02:27.233
"It sounds like your father was a great king," said Mandy.

40
00:02:27.253 --> 00:02:29.354
"He was.

41
00:02:29.854 --> 00:02:33.836
And he loved his people very much," replied the princess.

42
00:02:33.856 --> 00:02:37.418
"But Hangeul has not spread to everyone yet.

43
00:02:38.499 --> 00:02:40.520
Some people are upset by Hangeul.

44
00:02:41.521 --> 00:02:44.843
They say that learning is only for nobles and royalty."

45
00:02:46.283 --> 00:02:49.365
The princess pulled out a clean sheet of paper.

46
00:02:49.385 --> 00:02:53.808
"Now I will show you just how beautiful Hangeul is!"

47
00:02:55.012 --> 00:02:58.295
The princess poured water into the inkstone.

48
00:02:59.395 --> 00:03:04.979
Then she made ink, dipped a brush into it, and wrote two Hangeul letters.

49
00:03:04.999 --> 00:03:07.441
"Here you are."

50
00:03:07.861 --> 00:03:09.663
She gave the paper to Vinnie.

51
00:03:09.683 --> 00:03:12.545
"This says Vi-nnie.

52
00:03:12.865 --> 00:03:13.585
For your name!"

53
00:03:13.605 --> 00:03:15.547
"Thank you!"

54
00:03:16.087 --> 00:03:16.788
said Vinnie.

55
00:03:17.968 --> 00:03:22.772
Next the princess wrote Mandy's and Gildong's names in Hangeul too.

56
00:03:24.044 --> 00:03:26.546
Gildong was very pleased by the gift.

57
00:03:26.566 --> 00:03:28.688
"Thank you, Princess.

58
00:03:29.669 --> 00:03:30.790
I will remember this.

59
00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.812
I hope I get to learn Hangeul soon."

60
00:03:33.832 --> 00:03:38.476
"I think you will, Gildong," she said with a smile.

61
00:03:39.977 --> 00:03:42.419
Just then there was a sound at the door.

62
00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:45.762
A servant spoke in a worried voice.

63
00:03:45.782 --> 00:03:47.724
"Your Highness!

64
00:03:48.705 --> 00:03:49.806
The guards are coming!

65
00:03:50.766 --> 00:03:52.408
And they are looking for your friends!"
